/* book exam traps: Ec is not fck. For M25, fck = 25 N/mm² while Ec = 25,000 N/mm², a thousand times larger; both are in N/mm², which hides the slip. | The design stress of Fe415 is 0.87 × 415 = 361 N/mm², not 415 N/mm²; see partial safety factors. | For HYSD bars the design stress is reached at a strain of 0.87fy/Es + 0.002 (0.0038 for Fe415), not at 0.87fy/Es (0.0018). Using 0.0018 gives a wrong limiting depth of neutral axis. | Creep coefficients are 2.2, 1.6 and 1.1 for loading at 7 days, 28 days and one year; using 2.2 at 28 days overstates long-term deflection by 3.2/2.6 = 1.23 times. */
