/* book Worked example 2: Q: A beam 230 mm wide with an effective depth of 450 mm has 2 bars of 16 mm as tension steel. M20 concrete, Fe415 steel. Find its moment of resistance by WSM and the concrete stress when that moment acts.
   1. Ast = 2 × 201.1 = 402 mm²; m = 13.33.
   2. Neutral axis: 230x²/2 = 13.33 × 402 × (450 − x), that is 115x² + 5362x − 2,412,720 = 0, so x = 123.4 mm.
   3. Critical depth xc = 0.2887 × 450 = 129.9 mm. Since x < xc the beam is under-reinforced: steel governs.
   4. Lever arm z = 450 − 123.4/3 = 408.9 mm. MR = σst Ast z = 230 × 402 × 408.9 = 37.8 × 10⁶ Nmm = 37.8 kNm.
   5. Concrete stress at that moment, from the strain diagram: σcbc = (σst/m) × x/(d − x) = (230/13.33) × 123.4/326.6 = 6.52 N/mm² < 7.
   Answer: Under-reinforced; MR = 37.8 kNm, at which concrete is at 6.52 N/mm² and steel at its permissible 230 N/mm². */
