/* book exam traps: WSM uses the permissible stresses σcbc and σst, never fck or fy: for Fe415 the steel stress is 230 N/mm², not 415 or 361 N/mm². | The IS 456 modular ratio is 280/(3σcbc) = 13.33 for M20, not Es/Ec = 8.9; using 8.9 moves the neutral axis up and gives a different k, j and Q. | In an over-reinforced section the moment of resistance comes from the concrete, ½ σcbc b x (d − x/3); writing σst Ast (d − x/3) for it overstates the capacity. | In WSM the compression acts at x/3 below the top, so z = d − x/3; the 0.42xu of the limit state stress block does not belong here. */
